# Runs and captured artifacts. NEVER commit a captured run: it states, per server, where that
# server went and when, which is the who-calls-whom dataset this project says it does not publish,
# and gate rule 3 (docs/PROTOCOL.md) forbids a server, host or org name in anything published.
#
# The two exceptions below are not captured runs: they are REDACTED runs, produced by
# tools/redact_run.py, where every server id, tool name, destination host and address has been
# replaced by a stable label and every digest kept. They exist so `make n1` and `make reproduce`
# work in a clean clone with no Docker and no network, which is what the repository's own
# reproducibility claim promised and could not deliver. runs/README.md carries the three commands
# that prove they leak nothing, and tests/test_example_runs.py fails if they stop reproducing the
# published figures.
#
# The exception is by directory and by file: a run's disclosure.json and any other by-product a
# command writes into the directory stays untracked, so running the gates never dirties the tree.
/runs/*
!/runs/README.md
!/runs/example-sequential/
!/runs/example-concurrent/
/runs/example-*/disclosure.json
/runs/example-*/numbers.json
/runs/example-*/control/
*.pcap
!/runs/example-*/backstop.pcap
*.mitm

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Local CA material generated by mitmproxy. Secret by construction, never commit.
/harness/ca/
*.pem
*.crt
*.key

# The plan this repository was brought to its current state with. Untracked on purpose: it is a
# working document in Spanish, and the repository is English (a decision with its reason in
# CONTRIBUTING.md). What it asked for is in the commits, where it can be checked.
PLAN-*.md

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
